## Finding

**`dashboard/server.js:93`** — The `_ghCiCache` TTL guard `_ghCiCache.value !== null` defeats the 60-second cache whenever `gh` is absent, not authenticated, or returns an empty run list (all of which produce `result = null`). Because `null !== null` is `false`, the `fetchedAt` timestamp is written but never read on subsequent calls, so `execFileSync('gh', ['run', 'list', ...], { timeout: 15000 })` fires on every `/api/branch-state` poll.

The brief explicitly requires: *"Keep network/`gh` calls cheap and cached (short TTL) so polling doesn't hammer GitHub."* This bug directly contradicts that requirement. In the confirmed smoke-test environment (`gh` not installed), every dashboard poll performs a fork+exec that errors immediately — but still forks on every cycle.

**Fix:** Replace line 93:
```js
// before
if (_ghCiCache.value !== null && now - _ghCiCache.fetchedAt < GH_TTL_MS) {
// after
if (_ghCiCache.fetchedAt > 0 && now - _ghCiCache.fetchedAt < GH_TTL_MS) {
```

Note: `_getGitTips` uses `if (_gitTipsCache.value && ...)` which works correctly because its result is always a non-null object. Apply the same intent to `_getGhCi` by checking `fetchedAt` rather than `value`.

## All other ACs and quality checks: clear

All 8 ACs are satisfied. Intent achieved. Scope clean. No raw hex colors. No dead code beyond the finding above.
